    "created_at": "2012-11-20T16:03:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2012-11-20T16:03:16Z",
    "body": "(FWIW I imagine the right process here is for Lachy/the W3C have a git repo with two branches; one named whatwg that would have this as the upstream, and one named W3C. Then all W3C-specific patches would go in the W3C branch only and the process to update would be:\n\ngit fetch //Updates the WHATWG branch from its upstream\ngit rebase whatwg W3C //Rebase all the W3C-specific patches on the WHATWG upstream\n\nOf course you don't really need a whatwg local branch for this workflow, but it might make things more obvious.\n)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
